content.text:
Integrate WorkshopPage. Need import ProviderErrorDetails type, ProviderErrorCard. Add state. Need derive latest stored op error. Let's plan carefully.

At top imports:
```
import type { ProviderErrorDetails } from "../../shared/workflow.ts";
...
import { ProviderErrorCard } from "../components/ProviderErrorCard.tsx";
```
State:
```
const [providerError, setProviderError] = useState<ProviderErrorDetails | null>(null);
const [dismissedOperationErrorId, setDismissedOperationErrorId] = useState<string | null>(null);
```
In `act`:
```
setProviderError(null);
...
} catch (caught) {
 ...
 if (caught instanceof ApiError) {
   if (caught.providerError) {
      setProviderError(caught.providerError);
      setError(null);
   } else {
      setError(...)
   }
 } else setError(...)
}
```
`ProviderErrorCard` for transient and stored:
After project loaded, compute:
```
const latestProviderOperation = useMemo(() => [...(project?.operations ?? [])].reverse().find(op => op.providerError) ?? null, [project]);
const visibleProviderError = providerError ?? (latestProviderOperation && latestProviderOperation.id !== dismissedProviderOperationId ? latestProviderOperation.providerError : null);
```
But `project` may be null early; hook must be called unconditionally before early return. Current `activeRun` useMemo before early return. Add another useMemo before early return with optional. Good.
- `visibleProviderError` not hook.
- Render card in document:
```
{visibleProviderError ? <ProviderErrorCard error={visibleProviderError} onChangeModel={() => { setProviderError(null); setSetupOpen(true); }} onDismiss={() => { setProviderError(null); if (latestProviderOperation) setDismissedOperationErrorId(latestProviderOperation.id); }} /> : null}
```
- Avoid duplicate generic `error` when card visible. The `error` state set only non-provider. Also `abandoned` warning remains.
- If transient provider error and then project has stored op providerError, on dismiss transient, stored card appears. That's okay (persisted). Actually if the same operation has stored provider error, it may be the same details. Dismissing transient would immediately show stored card. Better onDismiss set dismissed ID to latest provider operation too. In button handler, both. Could define helper `dismissProviderError`:
```
function dismissProviderError() { setProviderError(null); if (latestProviderOperation) setDismissedOperationErrorId(latestProviderOperation.id); }
```
But latestProviderOperation is computed in render; handler can close over. Fine.
- If provider error is transient and no stored operation, just clear.
- If user performs another action and fails again with same operation? operation IDs differ. Reset dismissed? `act` clears providerError but not dismissed ID. If new op error id differs, card shows. Good.
- If reload page, dismissed state resets, persisted card appears. Good for evidence.
- Onboard screen early return: if error with providerError during onboarding? `act` not used there; Onboarding has own. No.
- `showOnboarding` early return bypasses provider card. Not relevant.

Add compact provider error line in RunInspector:
```
{operation.providerError ? <p className...>Provider {category}: {savedWorkChanged ...}</p> : null}
```
Could be good.

Also `WorkshopPage` line 232 "No paid model will be used." now false; update to "The app will not substitute another model." and warning section.

Also `engineSummary` warnings? The warning "selected model is not in catalog" no change. But if `selectedModel` exists and access policy blocked, `findSelectedModel` might return paid model; engine panel displays. Connection diagnostics show blocked. Fine.

Let's edit.

